3
00:00:16.741 --> 00:00:29.192
<v NARRATOR>Beside a jar of near-boiling water sat a small, weathered, unbothered creature, perfectly content in a heat that would end almost anything else.

4
00:00:29.192 --> 00:00:39.483
<v THRIVE>I am Thrive, and to me that scalding jar is a warm bath — I am an extremophile, a lover of the extreme.

5
00:00:39.483 --> 00:00:51.734
<v NARRATOR>Thrive gestured at the impossible places of the world — boiling springs, frozen ice, crushing trenches, water saltier than the sea.

6
00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:59.985
<v THRIVE>For almost every place you call impossible, some microbe has quietly moved in and called it home.

7
00:00:59.985 --> 00:01:10.436
<v THRIVE>The trick is never being generally tough — it is being precisely suited, with proteins built to hold their shape where yours would instantly unravel.

8
00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:20.967
<v NARRATOR>A microbe frozen in glacier ice slows its whole life almost to a stop, patient for a thousand years.

9
00:01:20.967 --> 00:01:32.298
<v THRIVE>When I was young I watched the microbes in the calm cool pond and thought they had it easy while I had it hard.

10
00:01:32.298 --> 00:01:40.509
<v NARRATOR>Then a cool-pond microbe drifted too near Thrive's spring one day, and the heat undid it in an instant.

11
00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:50.480
<v THRIVE>That was when I understood — my cruel spot was the one place I was perfectly, effortlessly alive.

12
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:59.291
<v THRIVE>Neither of us is tougher than the other; we are each fitted to opposite places, and mine is the one everyone else calls impossible.

13
00:01:59.291 --> 00:02:11.142
<v NARRATOR>Every time we find life where the world seemed too hot or too cold, we learn that impossible just meant nobody suited to it had arrived yet.

14
00:02:11.142 --> 00:02:22.273
<v THRIVE>So do not envy the cool pond — find the one hard place that fits you, and be the thing that thrives where nothing else even can.

15
00:02:22.273 --> 00:02:32.284
<v NARRATOR>Somebody has to live at the edge, and it may as well be someone strong enough to call it home. That is what makes Thrive Thrive.

